WEBVTT

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:15.410
Um...

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.360
Ah...

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.160
Uh...

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.660
Um...

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.800
So, it was a profession of love.
Well? What did he say?

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.000
Um... he said that we might not be
in the same class together next year,

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.140
so he wants an answer
from me by then.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.140
And? What will you tell him?

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.800
I'm not sure. No one's ever
professed their love for me.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.280
And I've never thought about
dating anyone before.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.450
"Wha...?"

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.410
- What?! What a waste!
- What?! What a waste!

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.640
Y-You guys!

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.180
Is he good looking?

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.620
He's in the soccer club!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:46.850
Sounds good!

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.420
"Why not?!"

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.530
Or is there someone else?

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.230
Will you profess your
love to this someone?

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.490
Um...

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.820
Uh...

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.430
Planning to Get Into Tokyo U Party

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.560
Apartment Manager:

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.560
Keitaro Urashima

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.880
<i>Tokyo U.</i>

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.210
<i>After I pass the secondary exams
tomorrow, I'll be a Tokyo U student.</i>

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.950
<i>And then I'll...</i>

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:22.590
Why am I going to all this trouble
to get into Tokyo U?

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:27.320
If I actually <i>do</i> make it in...

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.890
Then what?

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.360
Keitaro? Are you awake?

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.290
Can we talk for a minute?

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.070
Uh... Yeah, sure.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.080
Oww...

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.280
I'M SORRY!

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.280
Sorry.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.890
No problem!

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.420
Tomorrow's it.
The last test.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:01.490
How are you doing?

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.090
Um, pretty good, I guess.
How about you, Narusegawa?

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.570
I-I'm all set.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.300
We'll ace it together, then, right?

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.040
Right. Me and you
and Ms. Mutsumi.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.170
Hey, um, Keitaro...

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.140
That girl you made the promise to...
I wonder who she is.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:25.010
Maybe <i>you</i> were that little girl
I made it to, Narusegawa.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.460
Yeah, I thought the same thing.
You know, maybe.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.190
Room 201:

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.190
Shinobu Maehara

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.760
What am I gonna say
to Mr. Urashima?

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.270
That some boy professed
his love for me?

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.430
I can't say that to him!

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.870
But... But...

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.410
<i>But I have to say something.</i>

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:58.050
Narusegawa, it kinda feels like, I dunno,
it was fate that brought us together.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.880
Where did <i>that</i> come from...?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.560
Ow! My glasses! My glasses!

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.280
Sh-Shinobu!

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:24.850
I-I'm awfully sorry!

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.010
I came to talk! I didn't
mean to walk in on you!

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.810
I had no idea that the two
of you would be k-kissing!

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.450
What?! Naru and Keitaro
were smooching?!

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:35.980
Say <i>what?!</i>

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.750
What?! They're screwing
around before their exams?!

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.990
Urashima!
I'll cut you down!

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.690
Don't get too carried away, all right?

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:43.890
I didn't do anything!

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:13.740
Love Hina Spring Special

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.460
Tokyo U Secondary Exams, Second Day

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.570
All right! Today's the
moment of truth!

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.830
It's clinch time!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:30.470
Oh, my! Whatever were you two
doing up so late last night?

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:31.600
Nothing!

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:36.140
Be sure to read the instructions on
the question sheet very carefully.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.920
Please begin now!

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.560
<i>I understand this!</i>

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.900
<i>All of it!</i>

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.560
Yes!

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.870
<i>Four years of hard work
have finally paid off!</i>

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.270
<i>Now, if I can only score over 80%
on this killer English exam!</i>

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.610
<i>Wait, wait...
Calm down... Chill out...</i>

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.920
<i>The total score from my self grading
on the preliminary exams was...</i>

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.550
<i>The first day, I got...</i>

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:16.290
<i>No doubt about it! At this rate,
in the coming spring, I'll...!</i>

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:18.860
Keitaro Urashima

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.730
Keitaro...

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.070
You've finally followed
through on your promise.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.470
The groom may now
kiss the bride.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:35.900
Keitaro...

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:37.100
Na-Narusegawa...

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.270
I mean, <i>Naru...</i>

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.780
We're not about to let you be the
only happy person around here!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.940
<i>You</i> guys?!

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.320
Mr. Seta!

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.920
It's time we found out if you're
truly worthy of Naru.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.350
Get set!

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.530
You pack one helluva punch, Keitaro.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.910
I can entrust Naru to you.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.650
You just make sure
you make her happy, all right?

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:25.260
This time... no glasses.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.960
<i>Oops, I gotta watch it. I was so
confident I dozed off for a second.</i>

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.200
You have five more minutes.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:35.790
Five?

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:37.470
Wait...

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.300
Hey!

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.640
Just hold on...

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:44.470
...a minute here!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.110
Keitaro, how'd you do?

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:55.350
For me, it went off without a hitch!
No anemic fainting or <i>anything!</i>

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.690
Hey, Keitaro?

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.230
He's not here. Do you suppose
he's in the little boy's room?

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:06.670
"Please don't
look for me... 
- Urashima"

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.520
Wh-What the heck is this?!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.900
This is seriously too dangerous, right?

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.770
No sane person
would sign up for this!

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:13.640
Huh?

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:14.800
Keitaro?

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:18.470
This mess is all your fault because
you kidnapped Narusegawa!

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.080
What's done is done.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:25.250
Hey, check it out!

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:28.120
It's a help-wanted ad that was
posted at our university.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.960
"Manual labour, overseas, no experience
necessary, duration subject to change."

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:35.530
Ain't that fishy? You gotta wonder
what they'd make you do!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.890
Hey. Keitaro.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.500
<i>This must be the ship.</i>

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.440
<i>This time, I'm really
fed up with myself.</i>

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:55.010
<i>I gotta leave my lousy life behind.
Go overseas, to the middle of nowhere.</i>

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:57.280
<i>I'll start over from scratch.</i>

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.130
Maybe I'll start from scratch
somewhere else.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:14.870
Those here for the job, come aboard.
We're about to set sail.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.170
Wait! Stop!

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:20.900
I wanna get off, lemme off!
I don't wanna be here!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:33.720
Oh, forget it. Why should
I care anymore?

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.150
Huh? Is that you, Keitaro?

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:41.890
Mr. <i>Seta?</i>

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.820
We're bound for an island
called Pararakeke-something.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.600
According to the research of my mentor,
there's a strong possibility...

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.040
...that this place is where the ancient
turtle civilisation originated,

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.700
so we're going to excavate there.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:56.510
Boy, you seem awfully depressed.
What's wrong?

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:03.350
Well, it looks like I blew my chance
to get into Tokyo U again.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:07.820
I drifted off into fantasy mode
at the absolute <i>worst</i> time.

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.660
Hear me out!

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.260
Here.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.550
Why not give digging
another try, Keitaro?

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.560
I'll make sure you're well paid.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:22.330
Who knows? You might come across
something while digging.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.830
Right on!
I don't need Tokyo U!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:31.070
I can still lead a manly life like Mr. Seta,
traveling and digging around the globe!

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.120
<i>In which case, I won't be
needing these anymore.</i>

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:40.250
{1}Good-bye, Tokyo U.
Good-bye, Hinata Apartments.{2}

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.250
<i>Good-bye, Narusegawa!</i>

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:47.760
<i>Crap!</i>

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.530
Damn it!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.640
There's something on the back...

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.500
"Get into Tokyo U, Keitaro! ...Su"
"I hope you make it in... . Haruka"

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.850
"If you get in, I'll respect you... . Sara"
"We'll be Tokyo U students! ...Mutsumi"

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:07.810
"To Keitaro. Pass or fail, things won't
change between us, so take it easy."

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:14.420
Like I could ever
forget about them...

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:17.120
There's just too many memories.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.820
Come back!

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:26.100
Narusegawa!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.190
Huh?

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.430
You're sure in a hurry.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.670
We're still quite a ways off
from Parara-something Island.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:39.540
This can't be happening!

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:44.070
I'm gonna die
in a place like <i>this?</i>

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.090
Let's go to Tokyo U
together, okay?

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:50.350
Sure!

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:52.860
Promise?

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.750
I promise!

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:00.970
I... promise...

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.440
Pro-mees?

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.570
Pro-mees! Pro-mees!

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:11.810
Shinobu?

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.570
Shi-no-moo?

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.440
Nyamo.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.210
"Nyamo"?

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:21.420
Where am I?

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.170
Isn't it time you boys
started singing?

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.510
P-Please don't hurt us.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:44.770
We really don't know
where Keitaro went!

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.780
Let's set the stage for
Hinata Apartments'...

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.380
...most terrifying and
accomplished interrogator!

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:57.190
Must I? I don't like doing
this sort of thing, but...

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.730
Well... if it's Miss Haruka
who's doing it, I might not mind.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:04.730
Leave me out of your
twisted fantasies, pal!

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.400
N-Naru? C'mon, help us!

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:10.330
I swear, we don't know
anything about this!

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:12.970
Please let 'em have it.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.910
<i>Where'd that idiot
end up this time?</i>

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:20.270
<i>What about the promise he made to me?
Or doesn't he care anymore?</i>

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:21.910
Right.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.120
Hello, Hinata Apartments.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.660
Oh, Seta?
I'm a little busy right...

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:32.590
Keitaro <i>what?</i>

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:34.830
What's going on?!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.830
Is Keitaro with you right now, Mr. Seta?
Where is that idiot?!

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.760
What's he up to?!

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:45.670
I thought I saw him fall into the sea,
but it looks like he's on this island.

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:50.140
I'm amazed that he was able
to swim such a long distance.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:52.940
Mr. Seta, where's this
island you're on?

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:57.210
<i>It's called Parapara-something or other.
It's in the middle of the Pacific, about</i>...

00:12:58.390 --> 00:12:59.580
Mr. Seta!

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:02.790
Naru!

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:08.590
What're you doing?

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:11.390
Luggage? Wait, don't tell me
you're gonna go after him!

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:16.170
We're talking about Urashima. He no
doubt ran off again, just like last year.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:25.140
Ms. Mutsumi.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:28.740
Ms. Naru, aren't you interested in finding
out if we got into the university?

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.190
Could you find out for both of us?

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:34.480
I'm gonna go bring that
knucklehead home.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.100
You wanna go, too, Shinobu?

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:51.430
Well, I bet Mr. Urashima would be happier
if Naru went all by herself to get him.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:58.610
You and your wacky contraptions...

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.940
You're acting rather wacky, yourself.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.510
Aren't we friends?

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:05.420
I suppose I am Urashima's...

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:08.590
Well, we're getting pretty close.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:12.730
I'm guessing... this is
Pararakelse Island?

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.990
Tama? You came along?

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.630
It's a migrating flock
of hot spring turtles!

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.070
They <i>migrate?</i>

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:25.330
Do you have a better explanation?

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:27.710
Let's turn back.
We can't fly through this.

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:29.370
<i>What?</i> What's our location?

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:32.180
We're, um... over
Pararakelse Island...

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:32.940
Hey!

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:35.710
I'm gonna drag that blockhead home,
no matter what!

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:37.420
Thank you.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:51.090
Well, I suppose that's all the
screen time I'm getting this time.

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:56.460
How typical!

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.310
Tokyo U Entrance Exam Results Listings

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.440
I can't believe it!
There it is!

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:04.190
Mutsumi Otohime

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.510
- Yay!
- You're a Tokyo U girl now!

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.140
Happy new year!

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:10.440
I passed!
I made the grade!

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:13.850
Keitaro, Ms. Naru,
I finally did it!

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.760
Oh, no you don't!
Heaven can wait!

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.130
Show some muscle!

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:24.500
Ms. Mei?

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:25.730
There it is.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:28.630
Naru Narusegawa

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.900
Naru's name!

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.590
Well, I'll be!
Naru made it in, too!

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.530
Too bad Naru isn't here with us...

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.110
I'm so happy for her.

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.410
Okay, I guess we can
head home now!

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:41.850
We can't go yet! We haven't
found out how Mr. Urashima did!

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:45.910
But he fled after realising
that he would fail.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:49.820
Besides, we don't have his application
card. We don't know his number.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.430
I remember his application number.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.590
Let's see...

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:29.890
Welcome to Pararakelse Island

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:46.140
<i>Mr. Urashima wouldn't run off.</i>

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.680
<i>He said you can do anything
if you don't give up.</i>

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:52.020
<i>So I'm not going
to run away, either.</i>

00:16:56.220 --> 00:17:00.460
This "Pararakelse Island" here must be
the island that Seta was talking about.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.960
Even Naru's gone MIA now.
What's the deal?

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:06.100
Do you suppose... something
happened to them?

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:26.220
I want to be the first one
to congratulate my big sister.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.820
We're gonna go with you, Shinomoo!

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.950
Yay! A resort! A resort!

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:35.430
Sara? Su?
And you, too, Ms. Mei?!

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:38.830
Are you sure? If we go by ourselves,
they'll really chew us out.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.060
We're best friends,
right, Shinomoo?

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.130
Guys...

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.970
Let's find them
and bring them back!

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:53.610
Yeah!

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.440
Hold it right there.

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:56.910
Just like I figured.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:01.520
With nothing to go on, what could
you children possibly do overseas?

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:05.860
Ms. Naru will bring Urashima home safely,
so you needn't concern yourselves.

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.960
But what if the two of them
<i>don't</i> come back? What then?

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:12.660
Come back here.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.830
There's nothing you can't do!

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:18.270
You can do anything
if you set your heart to it!

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.140
That's what Mr. Urashima said to me!

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.710
Shinobu! Press the button on
your stuffed animal's forehead!

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:26.370
This?

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.380
Mecha Tama 3...

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:31.820
GO!

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:52.540
I can't believe that Su!

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.010
Well, shall we...

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:57.270
...get going?

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:59.540
What?! You're all packed
and ready to travel?!

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:00.640
You gonna stay behind?

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.610
No.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:04.480
I, too, am concerned
about Ms. Naru.

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:06.110
There's a problem, though.

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:08.350
I don't have enough for air fare.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:12.420
I have a plan.

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:26.730
The comic is finally finished.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:30.470
It's time to set out on my long-awaited
dream to sail around the world.

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:36.750
W-What's going on?!

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.280
Mr. Akamatsu?

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.980
We're gonna temporarily commandeer
your deluxe cruiser, the <i>Akamatsu,</i>

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.290
and chart a course for
Pararakelse Island, all right?

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:46.430
What? But this is the first
vacation I've had in...

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:48.430
You mean you don't
want to help us?

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.160
C'mon, talk us out of it!

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:52.860
I, uh...

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.100
Please, I can't do long lines!

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:09.740
What's going on?

00:20:57.470 --> 00:20:58.690
What is it, Tama?

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.030
<i>T-Tama?!</i>

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:01.530
Why, you little...!

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.870
What do you
think you're doing?!

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:12.710
That girl's name is Nyamo.

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:15.880
She's the granddaughter of my mentor
in archeology, a man I owe a lot to.

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:17.480
Where is he now?

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:21.190
He passed away.
Or he went missing, maybe.

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:25.450
See, about 10 years ago, he set out
to discover Paralantis, the lost city...

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:29.960
...of an ancient turtle civilisation,
located somewhere on these islands.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:31.790
He hasn't been heard from since.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:35.890
Nyamo's been living
in the jungle ever since.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:39.030
It looks like she and Keitaro
have hit it off nicely, though.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:41.300
I'm going.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.310
Naru, heaven only knows what's in the
unexplored jungles on these islands.

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:49.520
Don't worry. But there <i>is</i> someone
else you've been neglecting lately.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:51.040
Hey...

00:21:55.820 --> 00:21:58.820
Wow, I don't know what to say!
Oh, you've got it all wrong!

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:02.090
Haruka was still young back then!

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:04.160
Sara's mother was still with us, too.

00:22:16.410 --> 00:22:19.540
There. This ought to be enough
to get us across the desert.

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:25.780
Don't worry. I'll make sure
you keep your promise.

00:22:26.950 --> 00:22:28.650
My promise.

00:22:31.390 --> 00:22:32.190
What?!

00:22:32.230 --> 00:22:34.660
I finally found you, Keitaro!

00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:36.020
Narusegawa!

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.130
Time to go, Nyamo!

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:39.300
Come back here, you weakling!

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:44.200
Oh, no! The water!

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:49.230
A desert?

00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:55.840
Would you stop already, Keitaro?!

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:58.180
Why are you dragging
that girl into the desert?!

00:22:58.590 --> 00:22:59.750
I have to!

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:01.780
We're going to investigate
some mysterious jungle...

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:04.550
...that's supposed to be somewhere
on the other side of this desert!

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:06.790
The real question is,
what are <i>you</i> doing here?!

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:09.960
You just can't see the
obvious, can you?!

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:30.150
Let's go back.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:32.150
We have to find out if
we got into Tokyo U!

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:37.150
I blew it. It's pointless
for me to go back.

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:39.660
You'll never know for sure
unless you go see, right?

00:23:39.760 --> 00:23:41.690
Wrong. I know I screwed up.

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:46.720
I've just gotta forget about
Tokyo University and Narusegawa!

00:23:56.510 --> 00:23:57.770
Narusegawa!

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:08.180
This is Pararakelse Island?

00:24:08.220 --> 00:24:10.190
Now that we're here,
how do we find them?

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:14.580
That, Shinobu, is when <i>this</i>
little item comes in handy!

00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:16.990
But isn't that your <i>turtle</i> radar?

00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:21.130
I modified it to detect
Naru and Keitaro, too.

00:24:24.140 --> 00:24:25.160
That away!

00:24:27.510 --> 00:24:30.200
Mecha Tama 3... GO!

00:24:43.760 --> 00:24:45.520
So, this is Pararakelse.

00:24:45.560 --> 00:24:47.320
Think they have any sake
worth drinking here?

00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:49.520
Ms. Kitsune, that's not why we...

00:24:49.560 --> 00:24:50.550
I know, I know!

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:52.890
Thank you for all
your help, Mr. Akamatsu.

00:25:04.510 --> 00:25:05.530
Thank you.

00:25:08.210 --> 00:25:11.810
There's no more water, and we're
too weak to walk another step.

00:25:13.220 --> 00:25:14.210
Sorry.

00:25:14.320 --> 00:25:15.880
I'm sorry, too.

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:17.850
For saying I should forget you.

00:25:18.420 --> 00:25:20.290
I couldn't, even if I tried.

00:25:20.960 --> 00:25:25.260
Anyway, have you found
out if you passed yet, Naru?

00:25:25.930 --> 00:25:27.420
I still haven't...

00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:30.540
I haven't gone to see yet.

00:25:30.570 --> 00:25:32.230
Oh. I see.

00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:36.440
Uh... Keitaro, what happened?

00:25:47.190 --> 00:25:48.520
You dozed off?!

00:25:48.550 --> 00:25:52.620
I filled in all the answers in five minutes,
but I couldn't possibly have passed.

00:25:52.730 --> 00:25:56.680
That's why I felt so miserable.
I was too ashamed to face you guys.

00:25:57.160 --> 00:25:58.530
I see.

00:25:58.730 --> 00:26:00.890
And you call yourself a man?!

00:26:07.910 --> 00:26:09.270
Why, you little...!

00:26:18.080 --> 00:26:20.080
A mirage of Tokyo U.

00:26:20.490 --> 00:26:22.480
It's not Tokyo U...

00:26:23.060 --> 00:26:25.460
Huh? She speaks Japanese?

00:26:25.990 --> 00:26:27.150
No, wait.

00:26:27.360 --> 00:26:29.330
That's...! That's it!

00:26:47.580 --> 00:26:50.910
It's the mystery jungle!

00:27:01.790 --> 00:27:02.990
Hey, Narusegawa...

00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:10.090
Go and get the food ready!

00:27:10.270 --> 00:27:11.430
I'm on it!

00:27:14.940 --> 00:27:17.640
Hey, you know how to laugh.
Um..."Nyamo," right?

00:27:19.450 --> 00:27:20.410
Nyamo.

00:27:20.550 --> 00:27:22.450
What're we gonna do
about our clothes?

00:27:26.290 --> 00:27:27.270
Keitaro.

00:27:28.320 --> 00:27:29.750
Ta-dah!

00:27:30.690 --> 00:27:32.120
Leafy swim wear.

00:27:32.630 --> 00:27:36.030
This is simply out of necessity,
so don't get any funny ideas, pal!

00:27:36.230 --> 00:27:37.590
Too late!

00:27:38.560 --> 00:27:40.090
Those look delicious!

00:27:56.120 --> 00:27:57.280
Keitaro.

00:28:01.250 --> 00:28:03.880
I heard from Mr. Seta that Nyamo's
grandfather passed away.

00:28:05.190 --> 00:28:08.790
He set out to explore the interior
of this island in search of Paralantis,

00:28:08.900 --> 00:28:11.360
home of the ancient
turtle civilisation.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.130
Everyone thinks he died.

00:28:16.040 --> 00:28:19.160
Nyamo said she made a promise with
her grandfather that the two of them...

00:28:19.270 --> 00:28:22.440
...would search for Paralantis
together when she grew up.

00:28:24.940 --> 00:28:29.280
And now, she's trying to find
Paralantis on her own.

00:28:29.980 --> 00:28:32.780
She has complete faith that her
grandfather is waiting for her there.

00:28:33.090 --> 00:28:34.640
A promise...

00:28:34.750 --> 00:28:36.220
That's right.

00:28:36.460 --> 00:28:37.980
She's keeping a promise.

00:28:38.290 --> 00:28:42.490
So when I heard her story, it wasn't
all that hard to empathize with her.

00:28:42.660 --> 00:28:45.530
I botched my promise
to get into Tokyo U,

00:28:46.270 --> 00:28:49.170
so that's why I'm so determined
to help Nyamo.

00:28:49.440 --> 00:28:51.530
I want to help her
realize her dream.

00:28:51.970 --> 00:28:53.270
Understand?

00:28:53.910 --> 00:28:56.840
A-Are you angry with me?
Narusegawa?

00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:59.500
That's such a beautiful story...!

00:28:59.910 --> 00:29:03.110
Why didn't you share it
with me earlier?

00:29:03.420 --> 00:29:06.440
You know how sentimental I am
when it comes to promises!

00:29:06.920 --> 00:29:09.790
I'm gonna help!
We'll find Paralantis together!

00:29:10.360 --> 00:29:13.120
But what about finding out
if you got into Tokyo U?

00:29:14.330 --> 00:29:15.490
Don't worry about that.

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.300
Or don't you want me
to go with you?

00:29:21.170 --> 00:29:24.930
Sure, I'd be... thrilled.

00:29:28.240 --> 00:29:29.230
Narusegawa...

00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:32.140
Keitaro...

00:29:33.380 --> 00:29:35.140
Promise...

00:30:00.140 --> 00:30:01.130
I've got a signal!

00:30:01.810 --> 00:30:03.470
It's coming from that jungle!

00:30:04.640 --> 00:30:06.370
You mean that's where they are?

00:30:07.610 --> 00:30:10.100
We're going down!

00:30:20.360 --> 00:30:21.220
What the <i>heck?</i>

00:30:21.530 --> 00:30:24.190
I'm reading five... seven... <i>hundreds!</i>

00:30:24.360 --> 00:30:25.560
Say <i>what?</i>

00:30:25.830 --> 00:30:27.200
It's a flock of Keitaros!

00:30:27.330 --> 00:30:28.560
Or of Narus.

00:30:29.170 --> 00:30:31.470
No, the most sensible
answer would be...

00:30:32.940 --> 00:30:35.070
- A flock of turtles!
- A flock of turtles!

00:30:40.580 --> 00:30:42.850
- They're Mega Tamas!
- They're gonna eat us!

00:30:42.850 --> 00:30:44.820
HELP!

00:31:03.040 --> 00:31:04.530
<i>That looks like...</i> me?

00:31:13.510 --> 00:31:15.540
They just wanted to play.

00:31:15.980 --> 00:31:17.680
Don't be afraid.

00:31:19.790 --> 00:31:22.480
Oh, there you are, Nyamo!

00:31:22.790 --> 00:31:24.220
C'mon, let's go!

00:31:26.260 --> 00:31:28.060
<i>Wait, Mr. Urashima!</i>

00:31:29.130 --> 00:31:31.430
<i>Oh, no... I can't say it...</i>

00:31:37.070 --> 00:31:39.200
Are you sure it was the loser?

00:31:40.110 --> 00:31:42.470
Maybe it was just a dream.

00:31:42.940 --> 00:31:47.170
If Naru and Mr. Urashima are in this
jungle by choice, then maybe...

00:31:47.980 --> 00:31:50.810
Maybe we shouldn't chase
after them any more.

00:31:50.850 --> 00:31:51.870
Why not?

00:31:51.950 --> 00:31:53.580
Maybe we're butting in.

00:31:53.620 --> 00:31:56.880
And what if those turtles
decide to attack again?

00:31:57.790 --> 00:31:59.380
Either way is fine with me!

00:32:00.930 --> 00:32:04.230
We shouldn't give up!
We can do anything if we try!

00:32:05.130 --> 00:32:07.960
Isn't that something
Mr. Urashima told you?

00:32:08.670 --> 00:32:11.800
But he screwed up on his
exam and ran away.

00:32:12.540 --> 00:32:15.100
Sometimes trying isn't enough.

00:32:23.550 --> 00:32:25.310
<i>Keep on fighting, Shinobu!</i>

00:32:26.650 --> 00:32:29.090
No, no, no!

00:32:30.690 --> 00:32:35.960
I didn't come here
for Mr. Urashima <i>or</i> Ms. Naru.

00:32:36.860 --> 00:32:39.230
I came here because I wanted
to see things through!

00:32:46.670 --> 00:32:48.330
Shinobu...

00:32:49.980 --> 00:32:52.740
Missiles: Danger

00:32:53.310 --> 00:32:54.680
Hey, wait up!

00:33:12.400 --> 00:33:16.160
Just as I was singing a song,

00:33:16.870 --> 00:33:20.810
you were always
there with me.

00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:24.870
I felt a little embarrassed,

00:33:24.980 --> 00:33:28.210
but I was all happy inside.

00:33:28.250 --> 00:33:30.110
Go! Go! Go, go!

00:33:30.150 --> 00:33:34.180
Suddenly we were looking
at one another,

00:33:34.520 --> 00:33:38.390
and we doubled over
with laughter.

00:33:39.020 --> 00:33:42.650
You and I...

00:33:42.730 --> 00:33:45.930
...are like kittens playing
in the warm sun.

00:33:45.970 --> 00:33:47.870
Go! Go! Go, go!

00:33:47.900 --> 00:33:51.600
Some songs we
can't recall anymore,

00:33:51.840 --> 00:33:56.040
but if we sing along,
piece by piece,

00:33:56.840 --> 00:34:00.300
they come back into focus,

00:34:00.680 --> 00:34:05.120
along with promises
we shared with one another.

00:34:07.990 --> 00:34:16.400
Let's sing again,
anywhere and forevermore.

00:34:16.900 --> 00:34:20.300
We don't need memories,

00:34:20.500 --> 00:34:25.100
I just want to be with you
here and now.

00:34:25.670 --> 00:34:29.540
Because of the
friendship we share,

00:34:30.140 --> 00:34:34.100
there are songs
we can sing together.

00:34:34.580 --> 00:34:42.950
I didn't know that,
but I'm sure I was happy.

00:34:43.490 --> 00:34:52.060
Because of the friendship we share,
there are songs we can sing together.

00:34:52.360 --> 00:35:00.600
Oh, I truly know this now,
and I want to sing it to you.

00:35:01.310 --> 00:35:05.610
I am here for you,

00:35:06.150 --> 00:35:12.310
and I want to be with you again.

00:35:14.220 --> 00:35:15.620
A dead end?

00:35:18.960 --> 00:35:20.220
But we...

00:35:20.890 --> 00:35:22.330
But we came so far!

00:35:22.860 --> 00:35:24.420
How can this be?!

00:35:26.330 --> 00:35:27.230
Huh?

00:35:34.140 --> 00:35:34.970
Ow...

00:35:50.490 --> 00:35:52.720
Is this Paralantis?!

00:35:55.660 --> 00:35:57.250
Grandpa!

00:35:58.030 --> 00:35:59.550
Grandpa!

00:36:03.670 --> 00:36:04.930
Nyamo...

00:36:19.390 --> 00:36:22.380
There's nothing around here
except that little shrine we saw.

00:36:22.490 --> 00:36:26.290
I'm guessing that Nyamo's grandfather
didn't find what he was looking for here,

00:36:26.430 --> 00:36:28.830
and set out again
in search of Paralantis.

00:36:30.430 --> 00:36:32.330
You're going, aren't you?

00:36:33.500 --> 00:36:36.300
Yeah. I know it's Nyamo's dream,

00:36:36.540 --> 00:36:39.700
but I've sorta come to consider
it my personal quest, too.

00:36:40.170 --> 00:36:43.840
I might just stumble across ruins
that even Mr. <i>Seta</i> never heard of.

00:36:44.110 --> 00:36:46.540
Maybe I'll... go with you.

00:36:48.280 --> 00:36:51.840
What're you saying, Narusegawa?
You have Tokyo U waiting for you.

00:36:51.980 --> 00:36:54.820
I might've screwed up this year, too.

00:36:55.990 --> 00:36:59.790
That evening before we took
our secondary entrance exams,

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:02.290
I couldn't sleep a wink
because of what you said.

00:37:02.730 --> 00:37:06.690
I wasn't sure how well I did,
so I wanted you to come with me.

00:37:07.370 --> 00:37:11.600
I'm not sure if I want
to go back to Japan now.

00:37:12.470 --> 00:37:16.570
Because, well, if I went back,
and I <i>did</i> fail the entrance exam...

00:37:16.810 --> 00:37:18.870
Then there'd be
nothing there for me.

00:37:19.010 --> 00:37:23.740
But if I went with you and Nyamo and
chase after your dream, then maybe...

00:37:36.200 --> 00:37:37.180
What the...?!

00:37:37.600 --> 00:37:38.720
Nyamo, run!

00:37:42.730 --> 00:37:44.170
Naru! Keitaro!

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:47.440
What are <i>you</i> guys doing here?!

00:37:47.840 --> 00:37:50.600
Secret Arts!
Storming Flower Rhapsody!

00:37:53.180 --> 00:37:54.840
Missiles, fire!

00:37:59.490 --> 00:38:00.470
Are you okay?

00:38:01.250 --> 00:38:02.880
<i>Do</i> something, you doofus!

00:38:03.190 --> 00:38:06.280
I'm not sure what's going on, but we'll
back you up! Get in there, Kentaro!

00:38:06.390 --> 00:38:07.720
Roger that!

00:38:20.940 --> 00:38:21.840
Eject!

00:38:24.710 --> 00:38:26.080
Oops, we're outta missiles.

00:38:26.210 --> 00:38:27.340
Oh, no!

00:38:27.410 --> 00:38:28.470
Stay away!

00:38:28.980 --> 00:38:30.640
Stay away from me, turtle!

00:38:33.850 --> 00:38:35.550
You t-t-turtle!

00:38:36.360 --> 00:38:38.190
No, Nyamo!
It's too dangerous!

00:38:38.390 --> 00:38:40.020
Come down from there, Nyamo!

00:38:42.060 --> 00:38:43.050
It's her!

00:40:12.320 --> 00:40:14.480
Like I said, a migration.

00:40:24.430 --> 00:40:27.130
Oh, so that's the deal.
Now it all makes sense.

00:40:27.170 --> 00:40:29.030
What a heartwarming story.

00:40:29.370 --> 00:40:31.840
That's why we plan
to go with Nyamo...

00:40:31.970 --> 00:40:34.000
...and help her
search for Paralantis.

00:40:34.140 --> 00:40:35.870
Then take me with you!

00:40:36.040 --> 00:40:38.240
If you're going,
Naru, then so am I!

00:40:38.580 --> 00:40:39.700
Same here!

00:40:39.810 --> 00:40:42.440
In that case, it would seem
that you'll need a bodyguard.

00:40:43.650 --> 00:40:45.880
But... Are you sure?

00:40:46.250 --> 00:40:49.190
It's selfish of you to keep this dream
all to yourself, don't you think?

00:40:49.220 --> 00:40:50.690
We've come <i>this</i> far, after all...

00:40:50.960 --> 00:40:54.860
Besides, we might find treasure and
priceless artifacts in those ruins!

00:40:55.160 --> 00:40:57.220
Okay! Let's get going, everyone!

00:40:57.430 --> 00:40:58.090
Right!

00:40:58.130 --> 00:40:59.030
Nyamo!

00:41:00.170 --> 00:41:01.630
Man, she's raring to go!

00:41:02.930 --> 00:41:04.370
Wait, Nyamo!

00:41:04.440 --> 00:41:05.840
What's wrong?

00:41:08.340 --> 00:41:10.470
She doesn't want us to come.

00:41:12.140 --> 00:41:13.340
But why not?

00:41:13.480 --> 00:41:15.140
Why can't we come?

00:41:15.310 --> 00:41:18.750
We can't come with her
because this is Nyamo's dream.

00:41:18.980 --> 00:41:22.390
From this point on,
this journey is hers alone.

00:41:22.620 --> 00:41:25.280
She'll never make it by herself!

00:41:25.520 --> 00:41:28.820
Nyamo has faith that if she tries hard
enough, there's nothing she can't do.

00:41:30.560 --> 00:41:31.890
You do, too, Shinobu.

00:41:31.960 --> 00:41:34.020
But what about us?

00:41:34.270 --> 00:41:40.330
As dusk turns to night,

00:41:34.500 --> 00:41:38.560
No matter how wonderful it may
sound, it's not our dream.

00:41:38.870 --> 00:41:41.630
Seta has his dream,
Nyamo has her promise,

00:41:40.540 --> 00:41:45.070
small shadows jump about.

00:41:41.940 --> 00:41:44.070
and we shouldn't try
to make them our own.

00:41:45.540 --> 00:41:48.340
We have our own promises.

00:41:46.950 --> 00:41:52.610
They rush past me,

00:41:48.450 --> 00:41:52.820
All we have to do is find
our own dreams one day.

00:41:53.050 --> 00:41:54.680
After all, there's nothing
we can't accomplish.

00:41:53.220 --> 00:41:58.990
hurrying off to their homes.

00:41:54.720 --> 00:41:55.980
You're right, Mr. Urashima!

00:41:56.020 --> 00:41:57.780
Thank you, Nyamo.

00:41:58.020 --> 00:41:59.120
Shinobu.

00:41:59.520 --> 00:42:04.660
That day, you and I...

00:42:00.530 --> 00:42:01.690
Right.

00:42:01.730 --> 00:42:05.790
Even if we failed this time, we'll keep
on trying to make it into Tokyo U.

00:42:05.860 --> 00:42:10.670
...were at a place like this.

00:42:07.270 --> 00:42:08.630
Whaddya mean?

00:42:08.830 --> 00:42:11.030
Oh! Come to think of it,
we never told them.

00:42:11.400 --> 00:42:12.370
Dorks.

00:42:12.100 --> 00:42:17.540
We exchanged a promise there...

00:42:13.140 --> 00:42:15.660
Naru... Congratulations.

00:42:16.680 --> 00:42:17.660
You did it!

00:42:18.040 --> 00:42:26.720
...that was to be
our secret treasure.

00:42:19.680 --> 00:42:23.240
You, too, Mr. Urashima...
You made it into Tokyo U!

00:42:23.650 --> 00:42:24.440
Wha...?

00:42:25.610 --> 00:42:26.610
Keitaro Urashima

00:42:26.610 --> 00:42:35.570
Congrats!
You passed!

00:42:27.150 --> 00:42:28.190
Ya did good.

00:42:27.950 --> 00:42:35.120
Our precious promise,
made one heart to another.

00:42:28.420 --> 00:42:30.120
Congratulations, Urashima.

00:42:30.160 --> 00:42:31.920
You're in! You're in!

00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:35.790
Mr. Urashima?

00:42:35.390 --> 00:42:43.360
Even now, even now,
I hold it dear in my heart.

00:42:36.390 --> 00:42:37.520
Keitaro?

00:42:38.830 --> 00:42:39.800
Na...

00:42:39.830 --> 00:42:41.730
...rusegawa...

00:42:43.670 --> 00:42:49.400
Any day now,
we'll meet again...

00:42:43.970 --> 00:42:45.770
Snap out of it!

00:42:48.940 --> 00:42:50.200
I passed?

00:42:49.640 --> 00:42:52.470
...and I'll fulfill our promise.

00:42:50.240 --> 00:42:50.970
Yep.

00:42:52.640 --> 00:43:01.480
I live on, hoping
for that day to come...

00:42:54.780 --> 00:42:57.110
NARUSEGAWA!

00:43:01.550 --> 00:43:05.010
...any day now.

00:43:05.190 --> 00:43:06.420
Um...

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:09.920
By the way, you need to submit your
enrolment paperwork by tomorrow.

00:43:10.200 --> 00:43:12.430
Otherwise, your acceptance
is nullified.

00:43:14.100 --> 00:43:15.900
What?! By <i>tomorrow?!</i>

00:43:16.130 --> 00:43:17.860
We'll take Akamatsu's cruiser!

00:43:18.570 --> 00:43:21.040
A boat won't be fast enough!
To the airport!

00:43:21.210 --> 00:43:24.000
What?! But I don't
even have a passport!

00:43:28.980 --> 00:43:32.880
<i>You're not me.
I'm not as strong as you are.</i>

00:43:34.150 --> 00:43:36.950
<i>But I have all these
wonderful people with me.</i>

00:43:37.490 --> 00:43:41.860
<i>If you ever get lonely, please come
to Hinata Apartments anytime.</i>

00:43:42.790 --> 00:43:44.420
Shinobu!

00:43:51.100 --> 00:43:54.470
I'm sorry, but I...
I like someone else.

00:43:56.540 --> 00:43:57.510
Uh...

00:43:57.540 --> 00:43:59.600
He's in love with someone else.

00:44:00.150 --> 00:44:04.010
But I could never
hate him for that.

00:44:04.450 --> 00:44:07.780
I want to keep on liking him.
For just a while longer.

00:44:40.590 --> 00:44:45.250
I gaze up from the rooftops
and feel the surs warmth.

00:44:41.220 --> 00:44:42.280
Ms. Naru!

00:44:42.490 --> 00:44:45.950
Thanks for coming after us, Shinobu.
We never could have done it without you.

00:44:46.220 --> 00:44:47.690
I have to ask you something.

00:44:46.290 --> 00:44:50.790
Looking into the sky, you can feel
the energy building up inside!

00:44:48.660 --> 00:44:54.100
Um... How do you really feel
about Mr. Urashima, Ms. Naru?

00:44:52.260 --> 00:44:54.790
<i>That's so wonderful!</i>

00:44:55.070 --> 00:44:57.730
As far as I'm concerned,
that jerk is just...

00:44:55.100 --> 00:44:57.090
I feel so alive!

00:44:57.770 --> 00:45:02.500
I can't stop,
I can't ever give up!

00:45:02.710 --> 00:45:05.440
I'm saying goodbye to those
days when I felt so down.

00:45:05.540 --> 00:45:08.770
I've got these feelings
bubbling up from inside!

00:45:06.310 --> 00:45:08.750
He... He's just...

00:45:09.050 --> 00:45:13.850
You've gotta nurture those flowers
that'll bloom over and over!

00:45:10.120 --> 00:45:11.740
...someone I...

00:45:12.250 --> 00:45:18.810
...REALLY...

00:45:13.990 --> 00:45:16.680
It's comforting to run away
into your memories,

00:45:16.820 --> 00:45:19.920
but you've gotta break free
from them and live for tomorrow.

00:45:19.930 --> 00:45:21.150
...love!

00:45:20.290 --> 00:45:25.230
Your time to celebrate will come, but
you've gotta hold your arms out wide.

00:45:22.930 --> 00:45:25.230
...but you've gotta hold
your arms out wide.

00:45:25.260 --> 00:45:27.930
Days of struggle and turmoil
will go on and on,

00:45:28.100 --> 00:45:31.260
and you'll swing back and forth
between heaven and hell.

00:45:31.600 --> 00:45:36.540
You've gotta nurture those flowers
that'll bloom over and over!

00:45:36.570 --> 00:45:39.270
You've gotta run and run
until you find true love.

00:45:39.310 --> 00:45:42.370
Any pain along the way
is welcome news to me.

00:45:42.850 --> 00:45:48.050
Your time to celebrate will come, but
you've gotta hold your arms out wide.

00:45:48.350 --> 00:45:51.050
Stretch your arms out wide...

00:45:51.260 --> 00:45:55.060
...and hold those hands up high!
